course: dictionary
lesson: 1028
title: One word, two worlds: bookmark
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «A library book is kept dry, clean and away from food, and you use a bookmark instead of folding pages.» Here a bookmark is a real object you put in a book.
explain: Look at the words near the word. «Save» and «find it again» tell you the meaning is about computers: a bookmark on a phone or computer is a saved link to a website.
explain: Bookmark also works as a verb, a doing word. «To bookmark is to save a web page» means you are doing the action of saving. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or is someone doing something? That check helps you choose the right meaning.
fact: A bookmark is a strip of card, paper or ribbon you put in a book to show where you stopped reading.
fact: A bookmark on a computer or phone is a saved link to a website, so you can find it again quickly.
fact: To bookmark means to save a web page in this way.
fact: In library lessons, you use a bookmark instead of folding the corners of pages, because folded corners damage books.
fact: A library book belongs to everyone, so you keep it dry and clean and never write in it.
exercise: «You use a bookmark instead of folding pages.» What is a bookmark used for? | A ribbon to tie a parcel | A page folded down at the corner | A pen for writing notes in the margin | *A strip you put in a book to show where you stopped reading
exercise: Sam saves a website on his phone so he can find it again quickly. What is this called? | Folding the screen | *Bookmarking it | Printing the page | Deleting the app
exercise: «A library book is kept dry, clean and away from food.» What does the author want you to avoid? | Keeping the book clean | Keeping the book dry | Keeping the book on a shelf | *Keeping the book near food and drinks, which could damage it
test: «To bookmark is to save a web page in this way.» What kind of word is bookmark in this sentence? | A full stop | *A verb, a doing word | A noun, a thing | An adjective, a describing word
test: «A library book belongs to everyone: you sign or scan it out, never write in it, and return it by the due date because others are waiting.» Why should you return a library book on time? | Because you must write in it | Because the library closes at five | Because it gets heavier | *Because others are waiting to borrow it
exam: «A library book belongs to everyone: you sign or scan it out, keep it dry and clean, use a bookmark instead of folding pages, never write in it, and return it by the due date.» Which word means a strip you put in a book to show where you stopped? | scan | library | *bookmark | page
